## DESCRIPTION
##   Identify the Angle Between two Vectors
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by nhamblet

## DBsubject(Geometry)
## DBchapter(Vector geometry)
## DBsection(Cross product)
## Date(8/23/07)
## Institution(Union College)
## Level(3)
## KEYWORDS('Vector', 'Angle', 'Dot Product', 'Cross Product')

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Vector");

#  The vector u

@u = (random(1, 5), random(-5, 5), random(-5, 5));
$U = Vector(@u);

#  Vectors to test against

@V = (
    Vector(random(-5, 5), random( 1,  5), random(-5, -1)),
    Vector(random(-5, 5), random( 1,  5), random( 1, 5)),
    Vector(random(1,  5), random(-5, -1), random(-5, 5)),
    Vector(-2 * $u[2], 0, 2 * $u[0])    # perpendicular to this one
);

@dd = map {
    DropDown([ 'an obtuse angle', 'a right angle', 'an acute angle' ],
        $U . $_ == 0 ? 1 : $U . $_ > 0 ? 2 : 0)
} @V;

@shuffle = random_subset(4, 0 .. 3);

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

BEGIN_PGML

Suppose [`\vec{u} = [$U]`].  Then

a) [`` [$V[$shuffle[0]]]``] makes [_]{$dd[$shuffle[0]]} with [`\vec{u}`]. 

b) [`` [$V[$shuffle[1]]]``] makes [_]{$dd[$shuffle[1]]} with [`\vec{u}`]. 

c) [`` [$V[$shuffle[2]]]``] makes [_]{$dd[$shuffle[2]]} with [`\vec{u}`]. 

d) [`` [$V[$shuffle[3]]]``] makes [_]{$dd[$shuffle[3]]} with [`\vec{u}`]. 

END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();
